protesters are activists from Azerbaijan  they say their demonstrations aren't  political but Armenia is accusing them  of blocking the lasheen corridor the  only land link with a disputed enclave  and armenia's Parliament accused  Azerbaijan of causing a shortage of food  medicine and fuel for its 120 000 people  in nagorno-karabakh but the  demonstrators deny their blocking the  road they say they want a ban on what  they call illegal mining in the  mountainous region we are here  conducting this civil form of protests  in order to demand the right of  Azerbaijan to prevent the illegal  exploitation and the stealing of these  resources and here are Russian troops  tasked with a peacekeeping role Armenia  accuses them of failing to stop what it  calls an organized blockade  Armenia and Azerbaijan have been at War  twice over nagorno-karabakh most  recently in 2020 when Russia brokered a  peace deal an estimated 6500 people were  killed in that conflict on the sidelines  of a summit in Saint Petersburg earlier  this week armenia's prime minister made  a complaint to the Russian president  the most urgent issue is the crisis that  we have in the lachin corridor you know  for almost 20 days the corridor has been  closed off and this is a Zone under the  responsibility of the Russian  peacekeepers  the main question is the settlement in  the south caucases in general the  relations between Armenia and Azerbaijan  on the ground the situation appears the  same an independent news agency says it  saw a roadblock near a Russian  checkpoint it's understood that  civilians are being stopped from  returning to the enclave and one Aid  agency says it's been allowed through  with supplies Andrew Simmons Al Jazeera
 

